# Preserve behavior, not accidental implementation

Follow `/AGENTS.md` and the canonical contracts it names.

Always preserve product semantics, data meaning, persistence, security, owner/tenant isolation, entitlement, pricing, authentication/authorization, session lifecycle, navigation meaning, SPOMOVE runtime semantics, approved Product Decisions, and existing user-visible capabilities not approved for removal.

Do not automatically preserve DOM structure, CSS structure, component decomposition, spacing, width, font size, visual hierarchy, card/panel structure, responsive implementation, or expanded/collapsed presentation. When the user explicitly approves a design or redesign scope, those visual implementation details may change while behavior and capabilities remain intact.

Do not make unrelated changes. If an implementation exposes an unapproved semantic change, stop and report it through the Product Decision process.
